START

1. LOAD the image
   - Read "image.jpg" from the script's folder
   IF image not found THEN
       STOP with error
   END IF

2. PREPROCESS the image
   a. Convert image from color (BGR) to grayscale
   b. Apply Canny edge detection (thresholds 50, 150)
      → produces a binary image showing edges

3. FIND contours (shape boundaries)
   - Use cv2.findContours() on the edge image
   - This returns a list of all closed boundary outlines found

4. FOR EACH contour found:

   a. CALCULATE its area
      IF area < 200 THEN
          SKIP this contour (treat as noise)
      END IF

   b. APPROXIMATE the contour shape
      - Calculate perimeter (arc length)
      - Simplify contour into a polygon using approxPolyDP
      - Count the number of corners/vertices in the polygon

   c. CLASSIFY the shape based on vertex count:
      IF corners == 3 THEN shape = "Triangle"
      ELSE IF corners == 4 THEN shape = "Rectangle"
      ELSE IF corners == 5 THEN shape = "Pentagon"
      ELSE shape = "Circle"
      END IF

   d. GET bounding box coordinates (x, y, w, h) of the shape
      - Used to position the text label

   e. DRAW the contour outline on the image (green)

   f. WRITE the shape name as text near the shape (red)

5. DISPLAY the final image with all shapes outlined and labeled

6. WAIT for a key press

7. CLOSE all windows

END
